# v2.23 planning — 2026-10-31
# PROPOSAL-v2.23-backlog-2026-10-31.md (7a8c81f) and SPEC-site-audit-quarto-devmode-2026-10-31.md (#111; b1cb3b0,
# five decisions: auto from DESCRIPTION version, keep refusing PKGDOWN_DEV_MODE, mapper + pkgdown differential test,
# content_freshness unverified marker, allow only default vignettes/_quarto.yaml) are committed on dev. Proposed
# v2.23.0 = #111 + #114 decision. A fresh read-only adversarial review of the SPEC returned 2 blockers and ~10
# important findings (untriaged except two confirmed from the source: lib/_docsite.py:199 rejects a --site URL
# that differs from _pkgdown.yml url, which collides with the dev-base design; and the SPEC contradicts itself on
# whether a root URL is shifted or incomplete). Others to verify: inst/_pkgdown.* never read, PKGDOWN_DEV_MODE scan
# reads the working tree not the pinned SHA, bootstrap-3 dev sitemap prefix, a2_observations live-smoke gate and
# frozen A2 requirement rows, a differential test needs the Quarto CLI that A2 does not provision, freshness must
# reach the text verdict in lib/docaudit.py. Fix the SPEC before any code. Dev-base assumption (dev site = base shift) is unconfirmed:
# medfit has no /dev/ site. No code branch exists; created only on request. A2 re-attestation applies to _docsite changes.

