in_progress: nothing open. v2.22.2 released 2026-10-31 (PR #119 merge bcbfa57, tag v2.22.2; tap PR #248 merged). v2.22.1 released (exact short-integer comparison, #105/#106; PR #108 merge 6ce4e50; tag v2.22.1; tap PR #246). v2.22.0 released (A2 --site/--run-examples). Issue #101 closed: guardian guards tested, accepted limits recorded in COVERAGE-docs-check-a2-2026-10-12.md; integer comparator fix merged (#106, issue #105 closes at release). Post-release macos-14 guardian timing flakes fixed in tests only (64bf438, 80b12b7; dev CI 662/662 on both platforms). Post-release docs merged to dev: PR #95 (evidence vs approval guide, 709d92b) and PR #102 (evidence-bounded verification tutorial section, 32ee189); both unreleased.
  (1) #84 fix MERGED to dev 2026-10-11 as PR #85 (squash 99b4171; CI 5/5 green). #84 stays
  open until release (a feature→dev merge does not auto-close it). Follow-up PR #86 MERGED (squash f7036b4): a Codex
  adversarial review found #85 stopped /rforge:finish adding `version:` to a .STATUS that lacks one; fixed via
  lib.rstatus.version_overrides. Local worktrees feature-rstatus-version-drift and fix-finish-missing-version can be removed.
  (2) docs:check content audit, release A1 (v2.21.0): merged to dev via the feature->dev PR (see git log), UNRELEASED.
  lib.docaudit + /rforge:docs:check rewrite + dev-only replay harness (tests/harness/). SPEC and review record
  (TRIAGE-docaudit-signature-gate-2026-10-11.md) in archive/specs/; guide docs/guides/docs-audit.md. Seven Codex rounds under
  the stop rule; unrecognized R binding forms are documented known limitations. test-all 47/47, 44 commands.
  A2 (--site, --run-examples): MERGED to dev 2026-10-25 as PR #99 (merge commit 08ae163, so evidenced SHA 87525d4 is in history).
  Acceptance bound to 87525d4: RForge CI run 40151469287 (ubuntu-24.04 + macos-14, each 662/662 passed, 0 skipped, R 4.6.1),
  observations run 40153274868 (six passed), release aggregate run 40155770154 (verified true, 2 platforms). Limits: the adversarial
  review is attested (rounds 1-4 reviewed 661f9b5; 87525d4 differs only by the output-limit bound 15s->45s + manifest hash, delta_note
  in the record); live smoke supported-site is r-hub/cranlogs only (no Data-Wise/tidyverse package is checkable by --site).
  Planning files stay at repo root (tests/a2/requirements.json and scripts/verify_a2_release.py reference them).
next: triage the SPEC-site-audit-quarto-devmode review findings and revise the SPEC, then (on request) a feature branch for #111; delete stale local branches (user); brew upgrade rforge (user); optional real-package Codex rforge-lint CI-parity check.
