last_release_prior_v2_20_0: 2026-08-01 v2.20.0 (PR #71 feature/restore-finish→dev merge 8ae55cda — new
  /rforge:restore + /rforge:finish R-package session-boundary commands: recap a package's state
  (DESCRIPTION/NEWS.md/git/.STATUS) and sync .STATUS from what actually happened, dry-run by
  default with a redundant-edit guard and a version-drift check against DESCRIPTION. New
  lib/rstatus.py reader/differ module; apply_updates() helper added mid-review to close a
  data-loss trap (a bare RStatus(...) construction would have silently blanked every untouched
  .STATUS field on --write) — found by a 4-agent adversarial review before merge, along with a
  bare-# NEWS-header regex bug and missing control-char sanitization (both fixed). 42→44
  commands. PR #72 dev→main merge 362399d; tag v2.20.0; release
  https://github.com/Data-Wise/rforge/releases/tag/v2.20.0; CI green on main RForge CI + Deploy
  Documentation; dev synced back to main; live docs live-verified: 2.20.0. Docs sync bundled in
  the same release: REFCARD SESSION box section, docs/index.md What's New (was stale at
  v2.17.0-era content despite the version macro auto-updating — real bug, fixed), CHANGELOG +
  docs/changelog entries, command-cards/glossary/example-sessions (committed ab510af
  pre-release), and docs/lib-modules.md gained rows for sitelint/tidyaudit/rstatus — closing
  pre-existing table drift that had accumulated since v2.16.0/v2.19.0 shipped without updating
  it. Tap Data-Wise/homebrew-tap PR #197 MERGED b09762f — formula+manifest → v2.20.0, sha256
  157fa5ba…, generate.py --diff IDENTICAL. pytest 592 passed/2 skipped, test-all 42/44 (2
  pre-existing local-env-only failures: system python3.9 lacks 3.10+ union syntax, no
  mkdocs-material installed locally — both verified against dev baseline, unrelated to this
