  the formula's caveats/install-summary ("35"/"15 commands available", untouched by prior releases)
  and adopting craft's `command_count` + `{command_count}` template-token manifest pattern so future
  rforge releases only bump one manifest number instead of hand-editing the generated formula).
  Evidence-based `r:urlcheck` 403 triage (#67) — root-then-URL probing replaces the hardcoded
  `doi.org` heuristic; classifies dead/real_403 (gate) vs bot_blocked/transient (advisory),
  local-preflight-noise reduction only (does NOT fix CRAN URL NOTEs — CRAN's own check uses R's UA
  and can't be configured). `r:rhub` dispatch bugfix (closes #66) — `rhub::rhub_check()`'s first
  param is `gh_url`, not a local path (verified live against installed rhub — no `path` param
  exists); fixed via `setwd()`. `rc_submit()` did NOT have this bug (verified live before assuming
  symmetry — only the `rhub_check()` branch was broken). `_invoke_r` now folds stderr into failures
  instead of silently dropping them. New `r:tidy` command + `r:lint --tidy`/`--set-lintr` (closes
  #65) — tidyverse-conventions audit: tidy lintr preset, DESCRIPTION normalization preview/`--fix`,
  roxygen completeness (new `lib/tidyaudit.py`), NEWS.md header currency; all advisory, never block.
  Deliberately skipped the `r:cran-prep --tidy-audit` stage the issue itself marked optional.
  41→42 commands. pytest 558 passed / 0 failed / 2 skipped, test-all 44/44. Design record:
  PROPOSAL-url-403-triage-2026-07-16.md. Fixed a pre-existing test_version_sync.py bug the
