recent:
  - date: 2026-10-11
    branch: fix/finish-missing-version (PR #86 → dev, merged f7036b4)
    title: "fix(finish): add version from DESCRIPTION when .STATUS has none"
    state: MERGED to dev; unreleased
    summary: |
      Codex adversarial review of the docs:check SPEC/plan also reviewed #85 and found a regression: the
      drift-only `version` override left an existing .STATUS with no `version:` line "already current". Rule moved
      to lib.rstatus.version_overrides (fill when absent, correct on drift, keep matching annotated values); 5 new
      tests, negative control verified, pytest 615 / test-all 45/45. The review's other two findings were in the
      docs:check planning docs (unsatisfiable A1 recall gate; signature-arity flagging variadic functions) and are
      fixed in the feature worktree and logged in the SPEC as review 3 (findings 27-29).
  - date: 2026-10-11
    branch: feature/rstatus-version-drift (PR #85 → dev, merged 99b4171)
    title: "fix(rstatus): compare only the leading version token for .STATUS drift (#84)"
    state: MERGED to dev; unreleased (ships in the next release)
    summary: |
      build_recap compared the whole .STATUS `version:` string to DESCRIPTION, so an annotated line
      ("0.7.0 (released ...)") reported false drift (found on medfit). Now compares the leading token
      (v-prefix tolerated, 0.7.0.9000 still drift). The /rforge:finish recipe overrode `version` with the
      bare DESCRIPTION number unconditionally, which would have stripped annotations on --write; it now
      overrides only on drift. pytest 610 passed / 2 skipped, test-all 45/45, negative control verified.
