  - date: 2026-09-23
    branch: feature/status-phase-frontmatter → dev (PR #82, squash 9346070)
    title: "fix(status): take phase only from a phase: key in frontmatter .STATUS files"
    state: RELEASED v2.20.1
    summary: |
      lib.status took `phase` from the first "Phase X:" line anywhere in the file, so frontmatter
      .STATUS files (where such lines are history in the prose) reported a stale phase. Now
      frontmatter files read phase only from a `phase:` key; emoji-section files keep the regex.
      _apply_frontmatter returns whether frontmatter was found. +2 tests; review fix 18dcb05 names
      phase as the one field with no prose fallback in the docstring + regenerated
      docs/reference/status.md. test-all 45/45, pytest 604 passed / 2 skipped; CI 5/5.
